{% endif %}## Install

```sh
curl -fsSLo ~/.config/qutebrowser/acid-acetic.py \
  https://raw.githubusercontent.com/acid-theme/qutebrowser/main/acid-acetic.py
```

Then source it from `config.py`, which runs it with `c` already bound:

```python
config.source("acid-acetic.py")
```

Every one of qutebrowser's colour settings is set, so nothing falls back to a
default: the completion menu, context menu, tooltips, downloads, hints, key
hints, messages, prompts, the status bar in each mode, the URL in each state,
tabs including pinned ones, and the page background shown before a site paints
its own.

